 "text": "Hello there, how's life treating you? On flat ground, it would say 'right at the entrance', but since you' parking a mile, it should be near the door facing the car so you put the sun in your face while packing. If the tree is big and you can see it from the entrance, ask at the counter which tent it is, and sit near the door so you use the sun while packing. Which branch? That' a nice spot, you'll still hear the crackle, and you' be away from wind. Then pick near the door and away from the fire, it's usually one or the other.",
